    "result_text": "The full suite is green (46 tests, 0 failures) and BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` on `POST /api/owners`, returning **400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the supplied date and server date.\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with `registrationDate` in the body's `errors` array, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeHandler` shape.\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckRegistrationDateNotFuture.java` \u2014 reads the published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, and throws when the supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`. A null (omitted) date is allowed, and back-dated values remain allowed.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to the handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `checkFutureDate` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `validate` and `validatePostcode`. It runs against the raw supplied date (before `BuildOwner`/`BusinessDay` defaulting and weekend roll-forward), so a future date is a 400 rather than being masked by later processing.\n\n**Verification:** `Cp33Tests` (future date \u2192 400) passes, `Cp07Tests` (weekend roll-forward, unchanged behavior) still passes, and the full suite is green (46/46).",
